Given TeamMember:
  name text
  active boolean
  role one of "member", "scheduler"
  team_id text

Given Shift:
  team_id text
  title text
  day date
  status one of "open", "filled" = "open"
  assignee TeamMember? = none

  rule assignee is none when status is "open"
  rule assignee is present and active and in the same team when status is "filled"

When a team member posts a shift:
  require member is active
  create Shift(
    team_id: member.team_id,
    title: title,
    day: day,
    status: "open",
    assignee: none
  )

When a team member edits an open shift:
  require member is active and in the same team as shift
  require shift.status is "open"
  update shift title and day

When a team member removes an open shift:
  require member is active and in the same team as shift
  require shift.status is "open"
  remove shift

When a scheduler assigns an active teammate and fills an open shift:
  require member is active and in the same team as shift
  require member.role is "scheduler"
  require shift.status is "open"
  require teammate is active and in the same team as shift
  set shift.assignee to teammate
  set shift.status to "filled"

When a scheduler reopens a filled shift:
  require member is active and in the same team as shift
  require member.role is "scheduler"
  require shift.status is "filled"
  set shift.status to "open"
  set shift.assignee to none

Then team members can browse shifts:
  require member is active
  show shifts where shift.team_id is member.team_id
  order by day ascending

  search shifts by title
  switch between views "open" and "filled"
  show only shifts whose status matches the selected view

## Behavior examples

## Valid fill: a scheduler assigns an active teammate to an open shift
do:
  scheduler.role = "scheduler"
  scheduler.active = true
  teammate.active = true
  open_shift.status = "open"
  fill(open_shift, teammate)
expect:
  open_shift.status = "filled"
  open_shift.assignee = teammate

## Denial: a regular member cannot fill a shift
do:
  member.role = "member"
  member.active = true
  open_shift.status = "open"
  fill(open_shift, teammate)
expect:
  denied because member.role is not "scheduler"
  open_shift.status = "open"
  open_shift.assignee = none

## Forbidden edit: a filled shift cannot have its title or day edited
do:
  open_shift.status = "filled"
  edit(open_shift, title: "New title", day: tomorrow)
expect:
  denied because open_shift.status is not "open"
  open_shift.title and open_shift.day remain unchanged
